From bccb10d3bf2158dd141ed153876003975856eb04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayanng <johnenyenihi2017@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:46:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tts): add GMI Cloud text-to-speech provider

GMI Cloud serves Inworld Realtime TTS, MiniMax speech synthesis and Resemble
AI Chatterbox behind one multimodal request queue. Adds a GmicloudTTS
provider (ttsBuffer -> WAV buffer), the TTS_PROVIDER=gmicloud registry case,
settings mapping (TTS_GMICLOUD_*), settings UI with the provider picker
entry, and long-text handling: inputs are split at sentence boundaries under
the per-request text limit and concatenated PCM-wise into one WAV file.

Verified offline (14 behavior checks with mocked HTTP) and live against the
GMI Cloud API (inworld, minimax queued, 2528-char chunked request, bad key,
chatterbox voice validation).
